{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/reviews/id42394661"}, "name":{"label":"Sbianco"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2025-01-06T12:15:09-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"5"}, "im:version":{"label":"7.0.2"}, "id":{"label":"12153098654"}, "title":{"label":"Amazing!"}, "content":{"label":"This app is very good for teaching your kids. But there is some problems. Let’s start with the good things:\n\nFor my daughter, before she learnt how to read, she used this app, because I had hopes in it teaching her how to read. She used it, and it seemed there was no progress, for months on end she would just listen to the audio version of the books, until one day, she came up to me and said “mom, I wanna learn how to read.” \n\nI was so proud! This app gave the encouragement for her to learn how to read, seeing all the fun books, and she wanted to look at the pictures, without waiting for the audio of the book on that page to be done, and now she could both read, and look at the picture books, without having to wait!\n\nThis app teaches your kid creativity. When my daughters older brothers tried to stop her from using the creative activities, I didn’t even stop her from using them, and told her brothers to stop. And now, she’s one of the most creative kids I’ve ever seen! She’s covered a part of a wall in her room with her own drawings. To me, if this app made her more creative, just imagine what she will do next. She’s already planning on making her own YouTube channel!\n\nNow let’s move onto suggestions:\n\nWhat if you made tutorials on how to draw, write letters, and write sentences? You kinda already do that with the letters, but in the app, you have to write digitally, what if you made it so it doesn’t switch you to  the drawing activities, and you write with a pencil and paper while watching the app?\n\nNext, maybe you should make more age groups and grades? My daughter is now in fifth grade, and the app is only available ages 5-8. It’s really hard to find learning apps for a 5th grader, which isn’t just math, science, literature or other subjects, I want an app that’s all in one. Maybe you could make a few more grades for the app?\n\nNext, let’s move onto the problem:\n\nMy daughter, when she was in about 2nd grade, she kept switching her account to kindergarten. Maybe could you could make it so switching grades wasn’t so available to kids, and you can add a passcode on it, so they don’t switch the grades?\n\nOther then those, this is a great app! And I highly recommend it, wether it’s an after school program, or for homeschool, it can be for either. It’s a fun, easy, and educational experience, which I can confirm, belong in a school system.\n\nSo overall:10/10, would highly recommend this app.", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/review?id=1378467217&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"0"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"0"}}, 
